            "Regarding the cost efficiency of the previous works, it's usually convenient to collect extensive instruction-following instances with previous paradigms~\\citep{yin2023dynosaur,wu2023lamini}. Therefore, \\textit{is it worthwhile to try the proposed paradigm rather than simply gathering more instances from the other paradigms?} To answer this question, for all those baseline datasets from the ``direct comparison'' in Table~\\ref{tab:main_tab_t5}, we randomly sample subsets from them and train T5-3B on the subsets to show the performance trends (10\\\n",
